<h2><strong>Father&rsquo;s Day Customs and Traditions</strong></h2>
<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>The proclamation of making Father&rsquo;s Day a permanent national holiday was when U.S. President Richard Nixon signed it into law in 1972.</li>
<li>On the 40th day of Easter, Ascension Day, German men celebrate Father&rsquo;s Day by organizing hikes and other gatherings that are well-supplied with food and alcohol.</li>
<li>Father&rsquo;s Day in Russia is a celebration that has evolved from a military commemoration to an unofficial tribute to all men.</li>
<li>On Feb. 23, Defender of the Fatherland Day, parades celebrate the Russian Armed Forces while men can expect to receive small gifts from the women in their lives.</li>
<li>Father&rsquo;s Day is held in Brazil on the second Sunday in August in honor of St. Joachim, the father of Mary.</li>
<li>France owes its Father&rsquo;s Day celebration to a company that manufactured cigarette lighters.</li>
<li>In Thailand, men get canna lily (masculine symbol) flowers on Father&rsquo;s Day.</li>
<li>South Korea celebrates &ldquo;Parent&rsquo;s Day&rdquo; instead of Father&rsquo;s Day.</li>
